# BANAL: the shared docs that everyone touches. `merge=union` keeps both sides
# when two branches append different rows — the common case for Board J,
# CHANGELOG, and STATUS. Same-line edits (e.g. two branches fixing the same
# sentence) still need a human, but the parallel-cut Drive board no longer
# forces a rebase every time.
#
# Why not per-card generation yet? This one line is the 80% snack.
# The 20% is `Scripts/generate-board.sh` + `make board` which builds Board J
# from `docs/cards/J-*.md` Status lines — branches then never touch README
# by hand at all. Until that lands, `union` stops the hate.

docs/cards/README.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/STATUS.md merge=union
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=union
